    // ================= THE FROZEN GATE READER =================================
    // The manual's result for VMFL078 is Figure .78.2, "Comparison of X-Velocity
    // along the vertical centerline in the symmetry plane" (p.224, PDF p.238).
    // That line is x = 0.5, z = 0.5 (the cube's mid-span = the symmetry plane),
    // y running up the cavity.  This probe set IS that line, sampled at 201 FIXED
    // abscissae y = 0.005 .. 0.995 (uniform step 0.00495).
    //
    // WHY THE ABSCISSAE ARE FROZEN IN THIS FILE AND IDENTICAL AT EVERY LEVEL:
    // VMFL054 measured that the DEFAULT probe interpolation (the containing-cell
    // value) samples a slightly different physical location on each mesh of an
    // r = 2 family and POLLUTED the observed order (p ~ 0.21, GCI ~ 11 percent).
    // The fix, already paid for there, is `interpolationScheme cellPoint` plus a
    // frozen abscissa list -- so between levels ONLY the solution changes, never
    // where it is read.  This line is load-bearing; deleting it voids the triple.
    //
    // WHY THE WINDOW EXCLUDES y = 0 AND y = 1: those two points carry EXACTLY the
    // imposed boundary values (0 and 1 m/s) at every level.  Including them would
    // put an IDENTITY component into the gate functional (VERIFICATION_CHARTER
    // sec.2a: a quantity derivable by construction from its own inputs may be
    // reported, never gated on).  y_lo = 0.005 and y_hi = 0.995 sit strictly inside
    // the first/last cell at EVERY level (the finest, L3, has dy = 1/128 = 0.0078),
    // so no level is treated differently.
    centrelineProbe
    {
        type            probes;
        libs            ("libsampling.so");
        writeControl    writeTime;      // fires at the residualControl-terminated write
        interpolationScheme cellPoint;  // LOAD-BEARING -- see above
